.TH RGBDNS-SETUP 8 "2026-07-26" "rgbdns 0.2.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
rgbdns-setup \- configure a packaged rgbdns primary or secondary
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rgbdns-setup primary
.B --data
.I file
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B rgbdns-setup secondary
.BR --zone " " \fIname\fR " [" --zone " " \fIname\fR " ...]"
.B --primary
.I address[:port]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates the rgbdns service account and managed directories, writes service
environment files, and configures a primary or multi-zone secondary. It must be
run as root. Unless
.B --no-start
is used, the applicable systemd services are enabled and started.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --listen-ip " address"
Authoritative listen address (default: 0.0.0.0).
.TP
.BI --port " port"
Authoritative port (default: 53).
.TP
.BI --data " file"
Tinydns-format source file for a primary.
.TP
.BI --zone " name"
Add a zone transferred by a secondary. May be repeated.
.TP
.BI --zones " names"
Add a whitespace- or comma-separated list of zones transferred by a secondary.
.TP
.BI --primary " address[:port]"
Primary server used by a secondary.
.TP
.BI --allow-nets " cidrs"
Enable integrated AXFR for these comma-separated client networks. Transfers
use the authoritative TCP address and port.
.TP
.BI --query-log " bool"
Enable original-compatible per-request logging (default: 1). Use 0 to disable
it on a deliberately unlogged deployment.
.TP
.B --no-start
Write configuration without enabling or starting services.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rgbdns (7),
.BR tinydns (1)
